# Quick Difference Table

| Feature | `const` | `factory` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Object creation time | Constant when called in a const context; runtime calls also work | Controls construction; may return an existing instance |
| Needs `final` fields | Yes | No |
| Immutable | Yes | Optional |
| Reuse object | Canonicalizes equivalent constant instances | Only if explicitly implemented |
| Singleton | Does not enforce one instance of the class | Can implement a singleton; not automatic |
| JSON parsing | Rare | Common |
| Widget optimization | Yes | No |
| Existing object return | No | Yes |

---

### Interview memory line:

**`const` → immutable + compile-time + performance**

**`factory` → singleton + parsing + controlled creation**
